  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CuO</mi><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mover><mi>Cu</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>Copper oxide undergoes reduction to form elemental copper and water. This is a redox reaction. Since oxygen is removed from the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CuO</mi></math> it is undergoing reduction. And hydrogen&nbsp;is getting oxidised.</p>",
